From bc5cf34c680c898d2c7d9a974c848086df762024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Stackhouse <joseph.stackhouse@stack-tech.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:01:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] load independent GPU model contexts in parallel

Model load previously walked backend contexts serially, sharing one file
offset. This adds positional reads so independent backend uploads can overlap,
with one upload worker per GPU and host tensors loaded first, plus synchronized
progress reporting and finalization.

Cold-path readiness improved 51-59% against matched controls. Model load is
reported separately from inference throughput and is not a token-generation
gain.

Default-off, selected by LLAMA_MODEL_LOAD_PARALLEL=1, and eligible only without
mmap, direct I/O, or tensor checking. Deterministic output is retained.
